    {
      "filename": "Atkinson clock tower (11931846944).jpg",
      "title": "File:Atkinson clock tower (11931846944).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Atkinson_clock_tower_%2811931846944%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atkinson_clock_tower_(11931846944).jpg",
      "width": 2848,
      "height": 4288,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "Further down on the spine of rock that forms the Signal Hill Observatory is the Atkinson Clock Tower, which is seen here. More notes on that in subsequent captions, but the wooden tower really fascinated me. Like I'd never seen a tower made completely from wood before this! (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
      "dateCreated": "2013-11-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "atkinson-clock-tower-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "w94d",
      "mediumPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/atkinson-clock-tower-119318469-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/atkinson-clock-tower-119318469-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "It's a challenge to go around the tower (11931426775).jpg",
      "title": "File:It's a challenge to go around the tower (11931426775).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/It%27s_a_challenge_to_go_around_the_tower_%2811931426775%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:It%27s_a_challenge_to_go_around_the_tower_(11931426775).jpg",
      "width": 2848,
      "height": 4288,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "The splendid wooden Atkinson Clock Tower is perched at the edge of a steep hill, and it's quite a challenge to walk around it (though most visitors do). At one point (extreme left in this picture) the width is a mere ridge about a foot wide, so you need to hold on to the fencing real tight to avoid slipping down the steep, grassy hill into the traffic below. The Atkinson Clock Tower was for many decades used as navigation support for ships and is the oldest standing structure in Kota Kinabalu, but also the one of only three remaining buildings after the air raids in World War II.\n\n(Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
      "dateCreated": "2013-11-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "atkinson-clock-tower-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "w94d",
      "mediumPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/it-s-a-challenge-to-go-around--medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/it-s-a-challenge-to-go-around--small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "The wooden structure fascinated me (11931402055).jpg",
      "title": "File:The wooden structure fascinated me (11931402055).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/The_wooden_structure_fascinated_me_%2811931402055%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_wooden_structure_fascinated_me_(11931402055).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "The unique Atkinson Clock Tower is safely barricaded to prevent folks spraying grafitti or etching their names on it. The tower was built as a memorial to Francis George Atkinson who was the first District Officer of Kota Kinabalu. The Tower was built by his mother Mary Edith Atkinson in 1905. This Clock Tower has the distinction of being the oldest standing structure in the whole of Sabah that survived the destruction of Jesselton town during World War II. Till today, it still serves to keep the city's time. (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
      "dateCreated": "2013-11-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "atkinson-clock-tower-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "w94d",
      "mediumPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/the-wooden-structure-fascinate-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/w/9/4/d/atkinson-clock-tower-wp/the-wooden-structure-fascinate-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Reaching up to the sky (11931411565).jpg",
      "title": "File:Reaching up to the sky (11931411565).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Reaching_up_to_the_sky_%2811931411565%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reaching_up_to_the_sky_(11931411565).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "A final look at the Atkinson Clock Tower before we move on. To take this picture, I had to lie on my back and shoot looking back and up. I then inverted the picture while posting it here. Built in 1903, this all-wood, no-nails structure was built in memory of Francis George Atkinson- the popular first District Officer of Jesselton during the British North Borneo Chartered Company Administration. (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
      "dateCreated": "2013-11-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "atkinson-clock-tower-wp",
